  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "L001",
      "speaker": "ANNA",
      "text": "July 1969. Two cities, nine hundred kilometres apart, are waiting for the same signal.",
      "block": "0",
      "from": 15,
      "duration": 180,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L002",
      "speaker": "MAX",
      "text": "And nobody in either city knows that the *answer* is already sitting in a drawer.",
      "pauseAfter": 0.6,
      "block": "0",
      "from": 206,
      "duration": 193,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L003",
      "speaker": "ANNA",
      "text": "This is a demo episode. It shows how a script turns into scenes.",
      "pauseBefore": 3.5,
      "block": "0",
      "from": 522,
      "duration": 167,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L004",
      "speaker": "MAX",
      "text": "Every line of the script is one voice file. Every scene is anchored to a line.",
      "block": "0",
      "from": 700,
      "duration": 206,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L101",
      "speaker": "ANNA",
      "text": "Numbers get a counter. From two thousand five hundred down to seventy two.",
      "block": "1",
      "from": 917,
      "duration": 167,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L102",
      "speaker": "MAX",
      "text": "Dates get a timeline, and every milestone appears exactly when the voice names it: first January, then October, then December.",
      "block": "1",
      "from": 1095,
      "duration": 257,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L103",
      "speaker": "ANNA",
      "text": "Then and now is a split. Missing footage stays visible as a placeholder, so you always know what is left to find.",
      "block": "1",
      "from": 1363,
      "duration": 283,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L104",
      "speaker": "MAX",
      "text": "Rules and advice become a checklist.",
      "block": "1",
      "from": 1657,
      "duration": 77,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L105",
      "speaker": "ANNA",
      "text": "Who knew whom is a network: the founder first, then the partner and the rival.",
      "block": "1",
      "from": 1745,
      "duration": 193,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L106",
      "speaker": "ANNA",
      "text": "And the words of a real person become a quote, always with a source.",
      "block": "1",
      "from": 1949,
      "duration": 180,
      "file": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "L107",
      "speaker": "MAX",
      "text": "That is the whole idea. Write the script, anchor the scenes, check, render, watch, fix.",
      "pauseAfter": 1,
      "block": "1",
      "from": 2140,
      "duration": 193,
      "file": ""
    }
  ],
